@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+---
+id: dl-003-validate-the-entire-json-patch-document-before-applying-it
+type: decision-log
+title: "Validate the entire JSON Patch document before applying it"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+RFC 6902 defines a JSON Patch document as a JSON array of JSON objects. Validating only the members
+used by an operation allowed JavaScript-only values in ignored members, making a non-JSON patch appear
+valid. A same-location `move` also needs to validate its required source before it can be treated as a
+no-op.
+
+## Decision
+
+Validate and clone the complete patch document before evaluating any operation. Preserve the RFC rule
+that undefined operation members are ignored only after their containing operation has been established
+as JSON. Resolve the `from` location before treating a move to the same location as a no-op.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Patches that cannot be represented as JSON are rejected consistently, including when the invalid value
+is in an otherwise ignored member. Failed patch evaluations expose no partial mutation of the caller's
+document, and every move requires an existing source location.
