@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+---
+id: dl-004-represent-a-removed-json-patch-root-as-undefined
+type: decision-log
+title: "Represent a removed JSON Patch root as undefined"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+RFC 6902 section 4.2 permits removal of an existing target, including the root identified by the
+empty JSON Pointer. Rejecting this operation adds a restriction absent from the RFC. The JavaScript
+API needs a representation for the absence of a document that does not conflate absence with JSON null.
+The earlier root-removal restriction in pending dl-002 was never an approved decision.
+
+## Decision
+
+Return `undefined` when the root has been removed and not recreated. Keep this absent-document state
+distinct internally: root add may recreate a document, while operations requiring an existing target
+or source fail. Continue rejecting undefined as an input document or patch value.
+
+Implement replace as the RFC-defined remove followed by add, after checking that the target exists.
+This handles root replacement and prevents replacement from inserting extra array elements.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Callers can remove the root and distinguish the result from null. A root add can follow root removal
+within one patch. This return convention is a JavaScript API choice, not a representation prescribed
+by the RFC, and is documented in the README and API comment. Existing immutable evaluation preserves
+the supplied document and patch if any later operation fails.
+
+The implementation and regression tests are ready for review. All 19 repository tests and all 92
+enabled public JSON Patch conformance fixtures pass.
