+---
+id: task-003-conform-json-patch-to-rfc-6902
+type: task
+title: "Conform JSON Patch to RFC 6902"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+version: 2
+date: 2026-10-26
+---
+
+Reviewed `applyPatch` against RFC 6902 sections 3–5 and RFC 6901 pointer semantics.
+
+Implemented complete JSON patch validation, including ignored members and sparse arrays; checked
+the source of same-location moves; corrected array replacement to remove then add rather than
+insert; and supported root removal with an absent-document result and subsequent root recreation.
+The caller's document and patch remain unchanged on success or failure.
+
+Added red-first regression tests for the corrections and characterization tests for ignored JSON
+members, logical equality, pointer/index grammar, move ordering and prefix checks, copy independence,
+required operation members, and failure atomicity for every operation. Updated the README and API
+comment with validation, error, array, move, and root semantics.
+
+Validation: `npm test` passes all 19 tests (TypeScript compilation included). A separate comparison
+against the public json-patch/json-patch-tests suite passes all 92 enabled fixtures. Those external
+fixtures are not needed by the repository tests. `git diff --check` passes.
